00:37:07.770 --> 00:37:12.970
Climate change to the current day appears to have been a tug of war, really, between two man-made pollutants.

00:37:13.270 --> 00:37:18.800
On the one side, we've got greenhouse gases that are pulling the system towards a warmer state.

00:37:19.100 --> 00:37:23.790
On the other hand, we've got particles from pollution that are cooling it down.

00:37:23.930 --> 00:37:29.980
And there's a kind of tug of war going on between the two, in which the middle of the rope, if you like, determines...

00:37:30.000 --> 00:37:32.910
where the climate system is going in terms of warming or cooling.

00:37:34.670 --> 00:37:37.210
So which is stronger in the tug of war?

00:37:38.200 --> 00:37:42.060
Something powerful enough to push and pull on the global temperature

00:37:42.060 --> 00:37:46.540
has what scientists call a climate forcing effect.

00:37:47.540 --> 00:37:49.120
So as we're pumping up greenhouse gases,

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:52.120
we actually provide what's called a forcing on the climate system,

00:37:52.400 --> 00:37:56.570
a warming effect, which you can measure in terms of watts per meter squared,

